METHOD: Paste the following snippet into the console – it extracts visible text, normalises it, counts occurrences of a set of target keywords (`["лендинг","Пермь","за 2 дня","сайт"]`) and prints the raw count and percentage of total words.
```js
(()=>{const txt=document.body.innerText.toLowerCase();
const words=txt.match(/\b\w+\b/g)||[];
const total=words.length;
const kw=["лендинг","пермь","за 2 дня","сайт"];
kw.forEach(k=>{const cnt=words.filter(w=>w===k).length;
console.log(`${k}: ${cnt} (${((cnt/total)*100).toFixed(2)}%)`);
});
console.log('Total words:',total);
})();
```

